 "transcript": "Someone just released a free open source alternative to 11 Labs, and it runs completely on your own computer. It's called Voice Studio, and it's already sitting at over a hundred thousand stars on GitHub. It can clone a voice, design a brand new voice from scratch, dub entire videos with timed speech, transcribe audio, and even turn your stories into full audiobooks. And it works in 646 different languages. Now, the crazy part is that everything runs locally on your own hardware. So no monthly subscription, no character limits, and your audio never has to leave your machine. Even comes with a floating dictation widget, and it connects to your AI agents through MCP, so Clod can generate voiceovers for you directly. Normally, you'd be paying for 11 Labs, a dubbing tool, and the transcription app separately, but now it's all in one free tool. Just make sure you only clone voices you have permission to use. And to set it up, just open Clod code, paste in the link to the install guide, and tell it to install Voice Studio. It will detect your hardware, set everything up, and run a test generation for you. Comment Voice, and I'll send you the link.",
